.\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\panel_20260912_104522_xpadjud\kimi.txt:95:  Under a strict reading of the premise, `rd == 0` is `idata == k` with k=0 — the body never tests rd as a case — so it's disclosure. Codex's floor argument was "a bounded operand swap: an existing equality-to-zero predicate with the body-read index substituted" — i.e., treating it as an operand swap of some existing `== 0` predicate elsewhere in the function (e.g., `crm == 0`, `crn == 0` checks exist dominating the arm). Hmm — that's a stretch but defensible: the dominating predicates include `crm == 0 && crn == 0 && l_bit`; substituting rd for crn in an equality-to-zero yields `rd == 0`. That IS an operand swap drawn from... hmm, the swap source is a predicate, and the swap target field (rd) is body-read.
