.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260915_073005\kimi.txt:984:  4. Q3: no floor gap found. Small-edit sweep: every contracted class is rowed; the escapes that exist are (a) the (sw,+0x04) bypass — guest-equivalent, so not a behaviour undo; (b) value-bit×cell joints (e.g. `!(idata & 2)` at CONTROL 4W, `idata == 0x55` at +0x40 4W) — clause (e) by the project's own single-axis generating-set rule (joints are clause (e)); but DISCLOSED doesn't name the accept-side value discipline (the refusal side says it with all-ones stores; the accept side carries one value per cell and says nothing). Disclosed items: checked the "selection confined to zero bytes" equivalence against the lane math and the (uint32_t) TIME truncation — disclosed correctly. `goto → return 1` identity: correct (nothing between entry and tail writes HARDINT/SOFTINT).
.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260915_073005\kimi.txt:1001:  **Q3 — floor gap.** None found. The `(sw,+0x04)` bypass is guest-equivalent, so it undoes nothing the guest can see. Value×cell joints (e.g. `!(idata & 2)` at CONTROL 4W, `idata == 0x55` at +0x40 4W) do escape — the accept side carries one value per cell — but they are clause (e) under the project's own single-axis generating-set rule; the DISCLOSED list says this for the refusal side (all-ones stores) and for ENDIANESS latch effects, and does not say it for the accept side. All disclosed-equivalent items I re-derived (byte selections confined to zero bytes, the `return 1` identity, CONTROL 4R) are disclosed correctly against the lane math and the TIME truncation.
