.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260915_011138\kimi.txt:1147:  Now the floor-set derivation double-check — "the joint-cell rule (a dominating predicate crossed with the body-tested kind partition)":
.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260915_011138\kimi.txt:1281:  **Q1 — enumeration.** My independent derivation: kind partition = {8W, 8R, 4W-hi, 4W-lo, 4R-hi, 4R-lo} (the width arm's own branches); dominating predicates = the 6 case labels + default, the REV pc-window test, CONTROL's writeflag/DOG/leftover tests (HARD_RESET-true unrowable, disclosed). Floor = 40 cells: 24 label kinds (CONTROL's 4 realized as 2 reads + the value-0 writes), 4 window kinds (lwP/swP/sdP/ldP — complete since repair 11), 6 more CONTROL write cells (0x0201/0x0001/0x0200 × 2 widths), 6 default kinds. All 40 are present. No floor cell missing. No kind listed that the function cannot take (all 46 entries realizable on -M 64 ip32; the P kinds run from 0xbfc05180 with ra set in both sessions). Both fed rows (rearm once, latch x5) have live channels (count varies on second/suppressed announce; unclean on death).
.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260915_011138\kimi.txt:1311:  **Q1 — the enumeration.** My independent derivation from the function's branches: kind partition {8W, 8R, 4W-hi, 4W-lo, 4R-hi, 4R-lo} (the width arm's own `if`s), crossed with the dominating predicates — six case labels plus default, the REV pc-window test, CONTROL's writeflag/DOG/leftover tests (HARD_RESET-true unrowable, disclosed). That is 40 floor cells: 24 label kinds, 4 window kinds (complete since `ldP`), 6 further CONTROL write cells, 6 default kinds. All 40 are present in ACCEPTS; no floor cell is missing; no listed kind is one the function cannot take; both fed rows (`rearm once`, `latch x5`) have live channels. But "exactly that set plus the two named strengthenings" is **not exact**: 40 + 2 = 42 ≠ 46. The `("sw",0x04),("lw",0x04)` pair duplicates the 4-lo kinds already carried by the +0x34 pair (redundant); the `("sd",0x278),("ld",0x278)` pair duplicates 8W/8R but is the prologue's only accepted access with address bit 9 set — real, unrecorded strengthening work. Further, no ACCEPTS entry sets address bits 7 or 8, so a latch keyed on accepted-side bit 7/8 also passes — non-floor (no branch tests them), unrecorded. And the `cpu->is_32bit` true side of the redirect is an unrowable branch side no DISCLOSED bullet names (the HARD_RESET-true precedent says such sides are said).
