.\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\panel_20260913_061857\grok.txt:1:I'll start from the offloaded brief and the repo's current state, then read the crime width sources and kill-table artifacts before answering the three adjudication questions.The brief is loaded. Next I’ll read the crime access handler, the 71-row probe, and the kill-table artifacts so the dispositions can be checked against the tree rather than the packet.The probe and the width arm are in hand. Next I’ll list every row, the table-2 mutants, and the switch-side helpers so a joint cell the 71-row set doesn’t pin would show up.The 2-byte cells at INTSTAT/INTMASK/TIME look unpinned. I’ll confirm against the header and then measure that joint mutant in a scratch tree, not in `build/`.`only2r` leaves the INTSTAT/TIME 1-byte rows green, which is the hole. I’ll apply the joint mutant in a scratch clone and run the 71-row probe there.**GAP:** `goto crime_declined;` → `if (len != 2 || relative_addr != CRIME_INTSTAT) goto crime_declined;`
