rites were presumably 0xaabb via... hmm, in part 5 M_QUAL_GENCTL expected `rb2 genctl' 0xbb. But wait \u2014 in the row definition, rb2 genctl uses r6=\"0xaab8\" \u2192 lane (uint8_t)0xaab8 = 0xb8. But Section 10 says \"GENCTL reads 0xbb under the mutant\" \u2014 that was the Opus seat's own probe (101-row instrument), where the wide writes may have been 0xaabb. The part-5 prediction says \"M_QUAL_GENCTL -> `rb2 genctl' 0xbb\". Hmm! That's a discrepancy: if the probe's rb2 genctl session uses r6=\"0xaab8\" (as inlined in the diff), the landed lane would be 0xb8, not 0xbb.\n\nLet me check the diff: the rb2 loop: `(\"genctl\", GENCTL, \"0x82\", \"0x82\", True)` with `session(setup(r5=pre, r6=\"0xaab8\") + program([ST_B(5, off), ST_H(6, off), ST_H(6, off), LD_BU(4, off)])`. So two st.h of 0xaab8. On the mutant, the second lands 0xb8 into GENCTL. GENCTL's write body: stores idata (the byte) \u2014 `d->pcctwo_reg[relative_addr] = idata`? For GENCTL, the packet says \"GENCTL and MASK store the byte and reassert\". So GENCTL = 0xb8. Then `rb2 genctl` expected \"0x82\" \u2192 printed would be \"0xb8\" under mutant \u2192 red with value 0xb8, NOT 0xbb.\n\nBut PRETABLE Section 10's PREDICTIONS say: \"M_QUAL_GENCTL -> `rb2 genctl' 0xbb (and every other row green)\". And part 5 measured M_QUAL_GENCTL 117/118 rb2 genctl \u2014 the value isn't given in the table, just the red row. So the *prediction* of the red VALUE (0xbb) is inconsistent with the probe's actual session value (0xaab8 \u2192 0xb8), unless... hmm, wait. Let me re-check. Section 10: \"Non-equivalence shown on the saved binaries: after two wide writes GENCTL reads 0xbb under the mutant and 0x82 on the fix; MASK 0xbb vs 0x12\". That was the Opus seat's own measurement on ITS probe (the shipped 101-row instrument \u2014 it mutated and ran the shipped rows? \"at GENCTL alone and at all twelve: 101/101 both (own clone, the shipped 101-row instrument)\". But the shipped 101-row instrument has no rb2 rows \u2014 rb2 is the NEW row added in this 118-row diff. So the Opus seat's \"GENCTL reads 0xbb\" must have been its own ad-hoc check, with wide writes of 0xaabb. Then the PREDICTION \"M_QUAL_GENCTL -> `rb2 genctl' 0xbb\" carries the 0xbb from the Opus probe into the new row \u2014 but the new row's session writes 0xaab8, which lands 0xb8. So the prediction's red value is wrong; the red ROW is right. The part-5 measurement (117/118, rb2 genctl) presumably showed 0xb8. The packet doesn't show the actual measured value. So: the predicted red value 0xbb is inconsistent with the inlined session (0xaab8 \u2192 0xb8). Flag as a minor record defect (prediction vs row definition mismatch). It doesn't affect the kill (the row is red either way), but the record states a value the row cannot produce.\n\nHmm wait, let me double check the value written in rb2. `setup(r5=pre, r6=\"0xaab8\")` \u2014 and program: ST_B(5, off) [set byte], ST_H(6, off), ST_H(6, off), LD_BU(4, off). Yes, r6 = 0xaab8. So on the mutant the second st.h lands (uint8_t)0xaab8 = 0xb8. GENCTL stores the byte \u2192 0xb8. So `rb2 genctl` prints \"0xb8\". The prediction says 0xbb. Discrepancy confirmed. Unless GENCTL masks... GENCTL's arm: \"GENCTL and MASK store the byte and reassert\" \u2014 no mask. OK so 0xb8.\n\nAlso for MASK: rb2 mask session uses \"0xaab8\" too \u2192 mutant lands 0xb8; prediction in Section 10's own text: \"MASK 0xbb vs 0x12\" (Opus's probe). Fine, that's the Opus probe, not the row.\n\nSimilarly rb2 vecbase: pre=\"0x50\", two put h 0xaab8 at VECBASE. On mutant, second lands 0xb8 & 0xf0 = 0xb0 \u2192 VECBASE = 0xb0. Fix: 0x50. \u2713 (matches `rb vecbase own` expectation of 0xb0 under FALL).\n\nrb2 sccicr: pre 0x1f; mutant lands 0xb8 & 0x1f = 0x18. \u2713 red (0x1f expected).\nrb2 sccrx: 0xb8 & 0xdf = 0x98. \u2713 red.\nrb2 scsiicr: same 0x98. \u2713.\nrb2 t2ctl: pre 0x03; lands 0xb8 & 3 = 0... wait, TxCTL's body: `pcctwo_reg[rel] &= 0xfc; |= (idata & 3)` \u2192 RMW: from 0x03: &= 0xfc \u2192 0x00; |= (0xb8 & 3 = 0) \u2192 0x00. So t2ctl reads 0x0 under mutant vs \"0x3\" expected. \u2713 red. (want \"0x3\" \u2014 debugger prints... wait, rb2 for even blocks uses guest st.b readback (LD_BU then print r4) \u2192 printed value as the guest prints: \"0x3\"? The `want` is \"0x3\" \u2014 printed(t, \"r4\") presumably captures what `print r4` shows, which is 0x3 for 0b11. OK.)\nrb2 t2icr: pre 0x13; TxICR body: `&= ~0x17; |= idata & 0x17` \u2192 from 0x13: 0x13 & ~0x17 = 0x13 & 0xe8 = 0x00; |= (0xb8 & 0x17 = 0x10) \u2192 0x10. Expected \"0x13\" \u2192 red 0x10. \u2713.\nrb2 scctx: pre 0x1f; SCCTX body: per contract \"SCCTX\" \u2014 what does SCCTX store? Hmm, the contract's premise 5 lists arm bodies: VECBASE `& 0xf0`, SCCICR `& 0x1f`, SCCRX and SCSIICR `& 0xdf`, GENCTL and MASK store byte, TxCTL `& 3`, TxICR mask 0x17, SCCERR `= 0`. SCCTX isn't listed in premise 5! The rb/rb2 rows for scctx use pre 0x1f and want 0x1f, and the rb t2ctl note \"RMW at TxCTL: 0\" \u2014 for scctx, the diff's rb loop uses (\"scctx\", SCCTX, \"0x1f\", \"0x1f\"). If SCCTX's body masks or stores idata, a landed 0xb8 would give something \u2260 0x1f unless masked to 0x1f... The packet never states SCCTX's mask. Hmm, that's a premise I cannot settle from the packet: SCCTX's write body. The row's kill of FALL/DEL at SCCTX is marked M (part 1/2 presumably). \"SCCTX M\" in DEL/LEN \u2014 table says SCCTX DEL M (measured). And rb scctx row: set 0x1f, st.h 0xaab8 \u2192 landed (uint8_t) = 0xb8 \u2192 under FALL: whatever the body does with 0xb8. If body stores full byte \u2192 0xb8 \u2260 0x1f \u2192 red. OK, plausibly measured. Fine, M cells don't need my derivation.\n\nBut for the rb2 scctx row under QUAL: second write lands 0xb8; body stores/masks \u2192 presumably \u2260 0x1f \u2192 red. Part 5 M_QUAL_ALL measured: 107/118 with rb2 genctl, t2ctl, t2icr, scctx, vecbase, sccicr, sccrx, scsiicr, mask red (9 rows) + pscale noig2 + ipl noig2 = 11 red rows \u2192 118\u221211 = 107. \u2713 consistent: nine