.\regress\artifacts\lcaisalane\f2_8bd97e4_20260918\panel_20260918_190129\ollama_kimi.txt:12:The only rescue for E-DEBT available is to overturn F5's "each such a guard" by reading "any guard that declines a len > 8 WRITE" as intent-limited to cutoff-8-equivalent guards. REASONED: that rescue fails — F3/F4 are properly L4 because they were descriptive sentences false about the world; F5's sentence is the contract itself, and clause (e) exists to make headers mean what they say. Permitting intent-readings of overclaimed headers reinstates the laundering the escalation prong forbids. vc needs no special carve-out under this ruling, but note it is L2 even under the narrowest reading: lane is a body-read, body-distinguished operand (the parent's own 352 rows enumerate lanes as cells), so vc is a joint-cells floor breach independent of the contract wording. Agy's infinite-regress objection fails: the regress is capped by what the contract claims; had the header disclosed these as debt, debt they would be.
