.\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6286:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:22:**D1 — UPHOLD (e) / rows L1, and CORRECT THE REASON in the header.** Two different not-floor reasons were written as one. `} else if (d->dmaaddr & 0x1f)` keys on the body-read field — it is INSIDE DEPENDS-ON clause (2) — and is not floor because the body induces no partition of that field (joint-cells rule: *"a value or combination the body never tests as a case ... is DISCLOSED under clause (e)"*; the bounded form: *"the bits of the single value ... are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor"*). `!d->enable`, the static counter and `len` are OUTSIDE the enumeration (not body-read lvalues; `len` is the tail's argument). Opus's `if (X) -> if (X && Y)` shape argument is refuted by its own consequence: it makes `M_BIT30`, `M_EQ4` and `M_ZEROEXIT` floor too and kills the pass-1 and xscaleinten rules (grok). Grading by the consumer's tests is the transitive chasing the bound forbids. The shipped header's sentence *"the consumer-keyed forms (`enable`, the alignment bits, the read count) are outside the BOUND"* is an L4 wrong record on the alignment half — `d->dmaaddr` IS what the body reads. One-line fix.
.\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6288:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md-24-**D2 — UPHOLD FLOOR, REPLACE THE WARRANT; `case 0x00` is FLOOR.** "The complement of `== 0x04` is every other label" reaches the six labels and not the default-arm members (grok, glm). The warrant that does: the switch tests all eight bits of `relative_addr` by equality, so the (d) *mask-narrowed* generating set is one cell per bit — `& ~0x01` → 0x05, `& ~0x02` → 0x06, `& ~0x04` ≡ `case 0x00:` → 0x00, `& ~0x08` → 0x0c, `& ~0x10` → 0x14, `& ~0x20` → 0x24, `& ~0x40` → 0x44, `& ~0x80` → 0x84. Finite (eight), derivable from the diff, and the 35-row instrument rows ALL eight (seven `alias` rows + `other 0x14`). That answers ollama-kimi's "sampled to fit the submissions": it was at 29 rows; it is not at 35. glm's "the default arm is ONE cell, one representative suffices" is wrong on the carrier's own text — rows are owed PER ENUMERATED MUTANT, and each single-bit narrowing folds a DIFFERENT member. Two-bit merges are multi-axis joints: (e). One honest gap: `& ~0x10` and `& ~0x04` were never built as legs (predicted kills by `other 0x14` and `read val_a`); add both to table 5 so the generating set is measured, not two-thirds measured.
.\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6298:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md-44-**Outside the claim, disclose (not blockers):** a decline keyed on a sibling the consumer does not test — `} else if (d->timeout) { ... } else {` survives every read session (timeout is 0 in all twelve); the contract discloses sibling WRITES and `enable`, not sibling-KEYED effects — one clause. A post-copy side effect that sets a bit VAL_A already has (`d->dmaaddr |= 0x80000000;`) is invisible to the triple session; the contract claims only "clears", so no wrong record — two cheap rows (a second read in the `initial zero` and `read all ones` sessions) would close the single-bit generating set of that class; FILE or take, your call. Verified true: "no reachable 8-byte callback" (`fmov` with SZ=1 issues two 4-byte `memory_rw` calls, `cpu_sh_instr.c:789-795`).
.\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6355:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:13:**Q2 — row list, under my xscaleinten Q1 rule** (*"the floor is clause (b) verbatim reinstatement plus the dominating predicates' accept cell; every re-introduction keyed on a body-read operand the body does not test (`rd == k`, `field & bit`, `field == v`) is clause (e), disclosed BY CLASS; any row added for one is L1 — licensed because cheap, never graded floor because cheap"*). The body `odata = d->dmaaddr;` tests nothing; dominating predicates `relative_addr == 0x04`, `writeflag != MEM_WRITE`.
