.\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\panels\panel_20260924_115517\codex.txt:6587:GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\opus_p2.md:4:**VERDICT: RATIFY WITH REPAIRS — the diff itself is correct and I found nothing wrong with the seven arms or the delivery contract, but the 10-row detector has FOUR measured clean-sweep escapes (10/10), and one of them nulls the fix's own repair: `cpu->pc = 8 * vector;` (VBR dropped) is invisible to every row, while the diff's own comment and the probe's clause-(e) contract both claim VBR is delivered. That is an L2 floor breach plus an L4 wrong record; the `is_trap`/SFRZ joint cell is a second L2; the `dslot` row's SFIP channel is vacuous by construction (L3). All four repairs are one row or one constant each.**
